IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc1-common`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Part 2, entitlement: receiving education (regulations 12 to 14) and
-- accepting a claimant commitment (regulations 15 and 16).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, alone or as one of a couple.
--
-- The basic conditions in section 4(1)(d) (not receiving education) and 4(1)(e) (has accepted a claimant commitment) are the Act's.
-- The Secretary of State's judgments ("considers that", "specifies") are conditions: a plain input saying the Secretary of State
-- has reached that view or specified that day or method. Part 5 and Schedules 8 and 9 (piece uc4 and uc3) decide limited capability
-- for work: an input here.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 12: receiving education.

-- (1B) "Traineeship": a course (a) funded in whole or in part by, or under arrangements made by, the Secretary of State under section 14
-- of the Education Act 2002 or the Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding; (b) lasting no more than 6 months; (c) including
-- training to prepare the participant for work and a work experience placement; and (d) open to persons who on the first day of the
-- course have reached 16 but not 25. A course ending on the day 6 months after it began lasts no more than 6 months (fork F-ABS).
-- src:332 | “traineeship means a course which—
-- src:333 | (a) is funded (in whole or in part) by, or under arrangements made by, the—
-- src:334 | (i) Secretary of State under section 14 of the Education Act 2002, or
-- src:335 | (ii) Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding;
-- src:336 | (b) lasts no more than 6 months;
-- src:337 | (c) includes training to help prepare the participant for work and a work experience placement; and
-- src:338 | (d) is open to persons who on the first day of the course have reached the age of 16 but not 25;
@ref reg 12(1B) (src:332-338)
DECLARE `Course that may be a traineeship` HAS
    `the course is funded in whole or in part by, or under arrangements made by, the Secretary of State under section 14 of the Education Act 2002 or the Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts and Regulations (not a piece)
    `first day of the course`                                                                                   IS A DATE
    `last day of the course`                                                                                    IS A DATE
    `the course includes training to help prepare the participant for work and a work experience placement`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the course is open to persons who on the first day of the course have reached the age of 16 but not 25`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:332 | “traineeship means a course which—
-- src:333 | (a) is funded (in whole or in part) by, or under arrangements made by, the—
-- src:334 | (i) Secretary of State under section 14 of the Education Act 2002, or
-- src:335 | (ii) Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding;
-- src:336 | (b) lasts no more than 6 months;
-- src:337 | (c) includes training to help prepare the participant for work and a work experience placement; and
-- src:338 | (d) is open to persons who on the first day of the course have reached the age of 16 but not 25;
@ref reg 12(1B) (src:332-338)
GIVEN course IS A `Course that may be a traineeship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 12(1B) — the course is a traineeship` course MEANS
    (course's `the course is funded in whole or in part by, or under arrangements made by, the Secretary of State under section 14 of the Education Act 2002 or the Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding`)
    AND ((course's `last day of the course`)
         AT MOST (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` (course's `first day of the course`) (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months)))
    AND (course's `the course includes training to help prepare the participant for work and a work experience placement`)
    AND (course's `the course is open to persons who on the first day of the course have reached the age of 16 but not 25`)

-- (1B) "Relevant training scheme": a traineeship, or a course or scheme which (i) comprises education or training designed to assist
-- a claimant to gain the skills needed to obtain paid work (or more or better-paid work); (ii) is attended by a claimant falling
-- within section 22 of the Act as a work preparation requirement or as voluntary work preparation; and (iii) the claimant has been
-- referred to by the Secretary of State.
-- src:326 | “relevant training scheme” means—
-- src:327 | (a) a traineeship, or
-- src:328 | (b) a course or scheme which—
-- src:329 | (i) comprises education or training designed to assist a claimant to gain the skills needed to obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work);
-- src:330 | (ii) is attended by a claimant falling within section 22 of the Act as a work preparation requirement or as voluntary work preparation, and
-- src:331 | (iii) the claimant has been referred to by the Secretary of State;
@ref reg 12(1B) (src:326-331)
GIVEN `the course is a traineeship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the course or scheme comprises education or training designed to assist a claimant to gain the skills needed to obtain paid work, or more paid work or better-paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the course or scheme is attended by a claimant falling within section 22 of the Act as a work preparation requirement or as voluntary work preparation` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Act, sections 4, 5 or 22 (not a piece)
      `the claimant has been referred to the course or scheme by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 12(1B) — the person is participating in a relevant training scheme` `the course is a traineeship` `the course or scheme comprises education or training designed to assist a claimant to gain the skills needed to obtain paid work, or more paid work or better-paid work` `the course or scheme is attended by a claimant falling within section 22 of the Act as a work preparation requirement or as voluntary work preparation` `the claimant has been referred to the course or scheme by the Secretary of State` MEANS
    (`the course is a traineeship`)
    OR ((`the course or scheme comprises education or training designed to assist a claimant to gain the skills needed to obtain paid work, or more paid work or better-paid work`)
        AND (`the course or scheme is attended by a claimant falling within section 22 of the Act as a work preparation requirement or as voluntary work preparation`)
        AND (`the claimant has been referred to the course or scheme by the Secretary of State`))

-- (3) "Course of advanced education": a course of study leading to a postgraduate degree or comparable qualification, a first degree
-- or comparable qualification, a diploma of higher education or a higher national diploma; or any other course of study of a
-- standard above advanced GNVQ or equivalent, including above a general certificate of education (advanced level) or a Scottish
-- national qualification (higher or advanced higher).
-- src:342 | (3) In paragraph (2)(a) “course of advanced education” means—
-- src:343 | (a) a course of study leading to—
-- src:344 | (i) a postgraduate degree or comparable qualification,
-- src:345 | (ii) a first degree or comparable qualification,
-- src:346 | (iii) a diploma of higher education,
-- src:347 | (iv) a higher national diploma; or
-- src:348 | (b) any other course of study which is of a standard above advanced GNVQ or equivalent, including a course which is of a standard above a general certificate of education (advanced level), or above a Scottish national qualification (higher or advanced higher).
@ref reg 12(3) (src:342-348)
DECLARE `Course that may be a course of advanced education` HAS
    `the course leads to a postgraduate degree or comparable qualification`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the course leads to a first degree or comparable qualification`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the course leads to a diploma of higher education`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the course leads to a higher national diploma`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the course is of a standard above advanced GNVQ or equivalent, including above a general certificate of education (advanced level) or above a Scottish national qualification (higher or advanced higher)`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:342 | (3) In paragraph (2)(a) “course of advanced education” means—
-- src:343 | (a) a course of study leading to—
-- src:344 | (i) a postgraduate degree or comparable qualification,
-- src:345 | (ii) a first degree or comparable qualification,
-- src:346 | (iii) a diploma of higher education,
-- src:347 | (iv) a higher national diploma; or
-- src:348 | (b) any other course of study which is of a standard above advanced GNVQ or equivalent, including a course which is of a standard above a general certificate of education (advanced level), or above a Scottish national qualification (higher or advanced higher).
@ref reg 12(3) (src:342-348)
GIVEN course IS A `Course that may be a course of advanced education`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 12(3) — the course is a course of advanced education` course MEANS
    (course's `the course leads to a postgraduate degree or comparable qualification`)
    OR (course's `the course leads to a first degree or comparable qualification`)
    OR (course's `the course leads to a diploma of higher education`)
    OR (course's `the course leads to a higher national diploma`)
    OR (course's `the course is of a standard above advanced GNVQ or equivalent, including above a general certificate of education (advanced level) or above a Scottish national qualification (higher or advanced higher)`)

-- (2), (4) and (1A) Receiving education. A qualifying young person is treated as receiving education unless participating in a
-- relevant training scheme. Otherwise "receiving education" means undertaking a full-time course of advanced education, or any other
-- full-time course of study or training at an educational establishment for which a student loan or grant is provided for the
-- person's maintenance; and a claimant who is not a qualifying young person and is not on such a course is treated as receiving
-- education if undertaking a course of study or training not compatible with any work-related requirement imposed by the Secretary of
-- State. A qualifying young person who is in a relevant training scheme is not receiving education (fork F-12-SCHEME): paragraph (2)
-- opens "except in circumstances where paragraph (1A) applies", so (1A)'s exception leaves nothing to treat them as receiving it.
-- src:324 | (1A) A qualifying young person is to be treated as receiving education, unless the person is participating in a relevant training scheme.
-- src:339 | (2) Except in circumstances where paragraph (1A) applies “receiving education” means—
-- src:340 | (a) undertaking a full-time course of advanced education; or
-- src:341 | (b) undertaking any other full-time course of study or training at an educational establishment for which a student loan or grant is provided for the person's maintenance.
-- src:349 | (4) A claimant who is not a qualifying young person and is not undertaking a course described in paragraph (2) is nevertheless to be treated as receiving education if the claimant is undertaking a course of study or training that is not compatible with any work-related requirement imposed on the claimant by the Secretary of State.
@ref reg 12(1A), (2) and (4) (src:324-349)
GIVEN `the person is a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is participating in a relevant training scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is undertaking a full-time course of advanced education` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is undertaking any other full-time course of study or training at an educational establishment for which a student loan or grant is provided for the person's maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is undertaking a course of study or training that is not compatible with any work-related requirement imposed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 12 — the person is receiving education` `the person is a qualifying young person` `the person is participating in a relevant training scheme` `the person is undertaking a full-time course of advanced education` `the person is undertaking any other full-time course of study or training at an educational establishment for which a student loan or grant is provided for the person's maintenance` `the person is undertaking a course of study or training that is not compatible with any work-related requirement imposed by the Secretary of State` MEANS
    IF `the person is a qualifying young person`
    THEN NOT `the person is participating in a relevant training scheme`
    ELSE (`the person is undertaking a full-time course of advanced education`)
         OR (`the person is undertaking any other full-time course of study or training at an educational establishment for which a student loan or grant is provided for the person's maintenance`)
         OR (`the person is undertaking a course of study or training that is not compatible with any work-related requirement imposed by the Secretary of State`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 13: undertaking a course.

-- src:357 | (a) where a person has failed examinations or has failed to complete successfully a module relating to a period when the person was undertaking a part of the course, any period in respect of which the person undertakes the course for the purpose of retaking those examinations or completing that module; and
@ref reg 13(2)(a) (src:357)
DECLARE `Period of days` HAS
    `first day`  IS A DATE
    `last day`   IS A DATE

-- src:351 | (1) For the purposes of these Regulations a person is to be regarded as undertaking a course of education , study or training—
-- src:352 | (a) throughout the period beginning on the date on which the person starts undertaking the course and ending on the last day of the course or on such earlier date (if any) as the person finally abandons it or is dismissed from it; or
-- src:353 | (b) where a person is undertaking a part of a modular course, for the period beginning on the day on which that part of the course starts and ending—
-- src:354 | (i) on the last day on which the person is registered as undertaking that part, or
-- src:355 | (ii) on such earlier date (if any) as the person finally abandons the course or is dismissed from it.
@ref reg 13(1) (src:351-355)
DECLARE `Vacation during a course` HAS
    `period of the vacation`                                                                                                    IS A `Period of days`
    `the vacation is immediately after the last day on which the person is to attend or undertake the final module in the course that the person has registered to attend or undertake`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:351 | (1) For the purposes of these Regulations a person is to be regarded as undertaking a course of education , study or training—
-- src:352 | (a) throughout the period beginning on the date on which the person starts undertaking the course and ending on the last day of the course or on such earlier date (if any) as the person finally abandons it or is dismissed from it; or
-- src:353 | (b) where a person is undertaking a part of a modular course, for the period beginning on the day on which that part of the course starts and ending—
-- src:354 | (i) on the last day on which the person is registered as undertaking that part, or
-- src:355 | (ii) on such earlier date (if any) as the person finally abandons the course or is dismissed from it.
-- src:356 | (2) The period referred to in paragraph (1)(b) includes—
-- src:357 | (a) where a person has failed examinations or has failed to complete successfully a module relating to a period when the person was undertaking a part of the course, any period in respect of which the person undertakes the course for the purpose of retaking those examinations or completing that module; and
-- src:358 | (b) any period of vacation within the period specified in paragraph (1)(b) or immediately following that period except where the person has registered to attend or undertake the final module in the course and the vacation immediately follows the last day on which the person is to attend or undertake the course.
-- src:359 | (3) In this regulation “modular course” means a course which consists of two or more modules, the successful completion of a specified number of which is required before a person is considered by the educational establishment to have completed the course.
@ref reg 13(1) to (3) (src:351-359)
DECLARE `Course that a person may be undertaking` HAS
    `the course is a modular course`                                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `day on which the person starts undertaking the course, or the part of the modular course`                                IS A DATE
    `last day of the course or, for a part of a modular course, last day on which the person is registered as undertaking that part`  IS A DATE
    `day on which the person finally abandons the course or is dismissed from it`                                              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `periods in which the person undertakes the course to retake examinations or to complete a module after failing`           IS A LIST OF `Period of days`
    `vacations`                                                                                                                 IS A LIST OF `Vacation during a course`

-- src:352 | (a) throughout the period beginning on the date on which the person starts undertaking the course and ending on the last day of the course or on such earlier date (if any) as the person finally abandons it or is dismissed from it; or
-- src:353 | (b) where a person is undertaking a part of a modular course, for the period beginning on the day on which that part of the course starts and ending—
-- src:354 | (i) on the last day on which the person is registered as undertaking that part, or
-- src:355 | (ii) on such earlier date (if any) as the person finally abandons the course or is dismissed from it.
@ref reg 13(1) (src:352-355)
GIVEN course IS A `Course that a person may be undertaking`
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 13(1) — the last day of the period of the course or part` course MEANS
    CONSIDER course's `day on which the person finally abandons the course or is dismissed from it`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN course's `last day of the course or, for a part of a modular course, last day on which the person is registered as undertaking that part`
    WHEN JUST abandoned THEN
        IF abandoned LESS THAN (course's `last day of the course or, for a part of a modular course, last day on which the person is registered as undertaking that part`)
        THEN abandoned
        ELSE course's `last day of the course or, for a part of a modular course, last day on which the person is registered as undertaking that part`

-- src:352 | (a) throughout the period beginning on the date on which the person starts undertaking the course and ending on the last day of the course or on such earlier date (if any) as the person finally abandons it or is dismissed from it; or
-- src:353 | (b) where a person is undertaking a part of a modular course, for the period beginning on the day on which that part of the course starts and ending—
-- src:354 | (i) on the last day on which the person is registered as undertaking that part, or
-- src:355 | (ii) on such earlier date (if any) as the person finally abandons the course or is dismissed from it.
@ref reg 13(1) (src:352-355)
GIVEN course IS A `Course that a person may be undertaking`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 13(1) — the day falls within the period of the course or part` course day MEANS
    (day AT LEAST (course's `day on which the person starts undertaking the course, or the part of the modular course`))
    AND (day AT MOST (`reg 13(1) — the last day of the period of the course or part` course))

-- (2)(a) The period includes any period in which the person undertakes the course to retake examinations or complete a module.
-- src:356 | (2) The period referred to in paragraph (1)(b) includes—
-- src:357 | (a) where a person has failed examinations or has failed to complete successfully a module relating to a period when the person was undertaking a part of the course, any period in respect of which the person undertakes the course for the purpose of retaking those examinations or completing that module; and
@ref reg 13(2)(a) (src:356-357)
GIVEN course IS A `Course that a person may be undertaking`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 13(2)(a) — the day falls within a period of retaking or completing` course day MEANS
    (course's `the course is a modular course`)
    AND (any (GIVEN retaking YIELD ((day AT LEAST (retaking's `first day`)) AND (day AT MOST (retaking's `last day`))))
             (course's `periods in which the person undertakes the course to retake examinations or to complete a module after failing`))

-- (2)(b) The period includes any period of vacation within the period or immediately following it, except a vacation that
-- immediately follows the last day of the final module the person registered to attend.
-- src:356 | (2) The period referred to in paragraph (1)(b) includes—
-- src:358 | (b) any period of vacation within the period specified in paragraph (1)(b) or immediately following that period except where the person has registered to attend or undertake the final module in the course and the vacation immediately follows the last day on which the person is to attend or undertake the course.
@ref reg 13(2)(b) (src:356-358)
GIVEN course IS A `Course that a person may be undertaking`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 13(2)(b) — the day falls within a vacation that the period includes` course day MEANS
    (course's `the course is a modular course`)
    AND (any (GIVEN vacation YIELD `the vacation counts and includes the day` vacation) (course's `vacations`))
    WHERE
        `the vacation counts and includes the day` vacation MEANS
            (day AT LEAST (vacation's `period of the vacation`'s `first day`))
            AND (day AT MOST (vacation's `period of the vacation`'s `last day`))
            AND ((vacation's `period of the vacation`'s `first day`) AT LEAST (course's `day on which the person starts undertaking the course, or the part of the modular course`))
            AND ((vacation's `period of the vacation`'s `first day`) AT MOST ((`reg 13(1) — the last day of the period of the course or part` course) PLUS 1))
            AND (NOT (vacation's `the vacation is immediately after the last day on which the person is to attend or undertake the final module in the course that the person has registered to attend or undertake`))

-- (4) A person is not regarded as undertaking a course for any part of the period during which (a) they have, with the consent of the
-- educational establishment, ceased to attend because they are ill or caring for another person; (b) they have recovered from that
-- illness or ceased caring within the past year, but not yet resumed the course; and (c) they are not eligible for a grant or student
-- loan. "Within the past year" runs through the day before the same day a year on from the recovery (fork F-6-MONTHS).
-- src:360 | (4) A person is not to be regarded as undertaking a course for any part of the period mentioned in paragraph (1) during which the following conditions are met—
-- src:361 | (a) the person has, with the consent of the relevant educational establishment, ceased to attend or undertake the course because they are ill or caring for another person;
-- src:362 | (b) the person has recovered from that illness or ceased caring for that person within the past year, but not yet resumed the course; and
-- src:363 | (c) the person is not eligible for a grant or student loan.
@ref reg 13(4) (src:360-363)
DECLARE `Interruption of a course` HAS
    `the person has, with the consent of the relevant educational establishment, ceased to attend or undertake the course because they are ill or caring for another person`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `day on which the person recovered from that illness or ceased caring for that person`     IS A MAYBE DATE
    `day on which the person resumed the course`                                                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the person is eligible for a grant or student loan`                                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:360 | (4) A person is not to be regarded as undertaking a course for any part of the period mentioned in paragraph (1) during which the following conditions are met—
-- src:361 | (a) the person has, with the consent of the relevant educational establishment, ceased to attend or undertake the course because they are ill or caring for another person;
-- src:362 | (b) the person has recovered from that illness or ceased caring for that person within the past year, but not yet resumed the course; and
-- src:363 | (c) the person is not eligible for a grant or student loan.
@ref reg 13(4) (src:360-363)
GIVEN interruption IS AN `Interruption of a course`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 13(4) — the person is not regarded as undertaking the course on the day` interruption day MEANS
    (interruption's `the person has, with the consent of the relevant educational establishment, ceased to attend or undertake the course because they are ill or caring for another person`)
    AND (NOT (interruption's `the person is eligible for a grant or student loan`))
    AND (CONSIDER interruption's `day on which the person recovered from that illness or ceased caring for that person`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST recovered THEN
             (day AT LEAST recovered)
             AND (day AT MOST ((`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` recovered (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 12, unit IS months)) MINUS 1))
             AND (CONSIDER interruption's `day on which the person resumed the course`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                  WHEN JUST resumed THEN day LESS THAN resumed))

-- (1) to (4) A person is regarded as undertaking a course on a day if the day is within the period of the course or part, or in a
-- period of retaking or a vacation that (2) includes, unless (4) applies on that day.
-- src:351 | (1) For the purposes of these Regulations a person is to be regarded as undertaking a course of education , study or training—
-- src:352 | (a) throughout the period beginning on the date on which the person starts undertaking the course and ending on the last day of the course or on such earlier date (if any) as the person finally abandons it or is dismissed from it; or
-- src:353 | (b) where a person is undertaking a part of a modular course, for the period beginning on the day on which that part of the course starts and ending—
-- src:354 | (i) on the last day on which the person is registered as undertaking that part, or
-- src:355 | (ii) on such earlier date (if any) as the person finally abandons the course or is dismissed from it.
-- src:356 | (2) The period referred to in paragraph (1)(b) includes—
-- src:357 | (a) where a person has failed examinations or has failed to complete successfully a module relating to a period when the person was undertaking a part of the course, any period in respect of which the person undertakes the course for the purpose of retaking those examinations or completing that module; and
-- src:358 | (b) any period of vacation within the period specified in paragraph (1)(b) or immediately following that period except where the person has registered to attend or undertake the final module in the course and the vacation immediately follows the last day on which the person is to attend or undertake the course.
-- src:359 | (3) In this regulation “modular course” means a course which consists of two or more modules, the successful completion of a specified number of which is required before a person is considered by the educational establishment to have completed the course.
-- src:360 | (4) A person is not to be regarded as undertaking a course for any part of the period mentioned in paragraph (1) during which the following conditions are met—
-- src:361 | (a) the person has, with the consent of the relevant educational establishment, ceased to attend or undertake the course because they are ill or caring for another person;
-- src:362 | (b) the person has recovered from that illness or ceased caring for that person within the past year, but not yet resumed the course; and
-- src:363 | (c) the person is not eligible for a grant or student loan.
@ref reg 13 (src:351-363)
GIVEN `the day falls within the period of the course or part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day falls within a period of retaking or completing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day falls within a vacation that the period includes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not regarded as undertaking the course on the day by paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 13 — the person is regarded as undertaking the course on the day` `the day falls within the period of the course or part` `the day falls within a period of retaking or completing` `the day falls within a vacation that the period includes` `the person is not regarded as undertaking the course on the day by paragraph (4)` MEANS
    `within the period, a period of retaking or a vacation`
    AND (NOT `the person is not regarded as undertaking the course on the day by paragraph (4)`)
    WHERE
        `within the period, a period of retaking or a vacation` MEANS
            (`the day falls within the period of the course or part`)
            OR (`the day falls within a period of retaking or completing`)
            OR (`the day falls within a vacation that the period includes`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 14: exceptions to the requirement not to be receiving education.

-- (1)(a) The person (i) is undertaking a full-time course of study or training which is not a course of advanced education, (ii) is under
-- 21, or is 21 and reached that age whilst undertaking the course, and (iii) is without parental support (regulation 8(3)).
-- src:366 | (a) the person—
-- src:367 | (i) is undertaking a full-time course of study or training which is not a course of advanced education,
-- src:368 | (ii) is under the age of 21, or is 21 and reached that age whilst undertaking the course, and
-- src:369 | (iii) is without parental support (as defined in regulation 8(3));
@ref reg 14(1)(a) (src:366-369)
GIVEN `the person is undertaking a full-time course of study or training which is not a course of advanced education` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the age is asked` IS A DATE
      `the person reached the age of 21 whilst undertaking the course` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is without parental support` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(a) — the person is on a full-time course, under 21, without parental support` `the person is undertaking a full-time course of study or training which is not a course of advanced education` `date of birth` `the day on which the age is asked` `the person reached the age of 21 whilst undertaking the course` `the person is without parental support` MEANS
    (`the person is undertaking a full-time course of study or training which is not a course of advanced education`)
    AND (`under 21, or 21 and reached that age whilst undertaking the course`)
    AND (`the person is without parental support`)
    WHERE
        `under 21, or 21 and reached that age whilst undertaking the course` MEANS
            (`uc1 — the age in complete years on a date` `date of birth` `the day on which the age is asked` LESS THAN 21)
            OR ((`uc1 — the age in complete years on a date` `date of birth` `the day on which the age is asked` EQUALS 21)
                AND (`the person reached the age of 21 whilst undertaking the course`))

-- (1)(b) The person is entitled to attendance allowance, pension age disability payment, disability living allowance, Scottish adult
-- disability living allowance, child disability payment, adult disability payment or personal independence payment and, on a date before
-- the date on which they start receiving education, (i) it was determined that they have limited capability for work, or for work and
-- work-related activity, on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 or Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations; or (ii) they were treated
-- as having limited capability for work under Schedule 8 or limited capability for work and work-related activity under Schedule 9.
-- src:370 | (b) the person is entitled to attendance allowance , pension age disability payment, disability living allowance , Scottish adult disability living allowance, child disability payment , adult disability payment or personal independence payment and, on a date before the date on which the person starts receiving education—
-- src:371 | (i) it has been determined that the person has limited capability for work or limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations; or
-- src:372 | (ii) the person is treated as having limited capability for work under Schedule 8 or limited capability for work and work-related activity under Schedule 9;
@ref reg 14(1)(b) (src:370-372)
GIVEN entitled IS A LIST OF Benefit
      `before the person started receiving education it was determined that the person has limited capability for work or limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Part 5 (piece uc4)
      `before the person started receiving education the person was treated as having limited capability for work under Schedule 8 or limited capability for work and work-related activity under Schedule 9` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Schedules 8 and 9 (piece uc4)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(b) — the person is entitled to a disability benefit and was found to have limited capability for work` entitled `before the person started receiving education it was determined that the person has limited capability for work or limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations` `before the person started receiving education the person was treated as having limited capability for work under Schedule 8 or limited capability for work and work-related activity under Schedule 9` MEANS
    `entitled to one of the benefits`
    AND (`before the person started receiving education it was determined that the person has limited capability for work or limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations`
         OR `before the person started receiving education the person was treated as having limited capability for work under Schedule 8 or limited capability for work and work-related activity under Schedule 9`)
    WHERE
        `entitled to one of the benefits` MEANS
            (elem `attendance allowance` entitled)
            OR (elem `pension age disability payment` entitled)
            OR (elem `disability living allowance` entitled)
            OR (elem `Scottish adult disability living allowance` entitled)
            OR (elem `child disability payment` entitled)
            OR (elem `adult disability payment` entitled)
            OR (elem `personal independence payment` entitled)

-- (1)(e) A member of a couple, both of whom are receiving education, and the other member is (i) responsible for a child or qualifying
-- young person, or (ii) a foster parent with whom a child is placed.
-- src:375 | (e) the person is a member of a couple, both of whom are receiving education, and the other member is—
-- src:376 | (i) responsible for a child or qualifying young person, or
-- src:377 | (ii) a foster parent with whom a child is placed; or
@ref reg 14(1)(e) (src:375-377)
GIVEN `the person is a member of a couple, both of whom are receiving education` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other member is responsible for a child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other member is a foster parent with whom a child is placed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(e) — both members of the couple are receiving education and the other is responsible for a child or is a foster parent` `the person is a member of a couple, both of whom are receiving education` `the other member is responsible for a child or qualifying young person` `the other member is a foster parent with whom a child is placed` MEANS
    (`the person is a member of a couple, both of whom are receiving education`)
    AND ((`the other member is responsible for a child or qualifying young person`)
         OR (`the other member is a foster parent with whom a child is placed`))

-- (1) A person does not have to meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(d) if (a) to (f): (c) responsible for a child or qualifying
-- young person; (d) a single person and a foster parent with whom a child is placed; (f) has reached the qualifying age for state
-- pension credit and is a member of a couple the other member of which has not.
-- src:365 | (1) A person does not have to meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(d) of the Act (not receiving education) if—
-- src:373 | (c) the person is responsible for a child or a qualifying young person;
-- src:374 | (d) the person is a single person and a foster parent with whom a child is placed;
-- src:378 | (f) the person—
-- src:379 | (i) has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit, and
-- src:380 | (ii) is a member of a couple the other member of which has not reached that age.
@ref reg 14(1) (src:365-380)
GIVEN `the person falls within sub-paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person falls within sub-paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is responsible for a child or a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a single person and a foster parent with whom a child is placed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person falls within sub-paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of a couple the other member of which has not reached that age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1) — the person is excepted from the basic condition in section 4(1)(d)` `the person falls within sub-paragraph (a)` `the person falls within sub-paragraph (b)` `the person is responsible for a child or a qualifying young person` `the person is a single person and a foster parent with whom a child is placed` `the person falls within sub-paragraph (e)` `the person has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` `the person is a member of a couple the other member of which has not reached that age` MEANS
    `the person falls within sub-paragraph (a)`
    OR `the person falls within sub-paragraph (b)`
    OR `the person is responsible for a child or a qualifying young person`
    OR `the person is a single person and a foster parent with whom a child is placed`
    OR `the person falls within sub-paragraph (e)`
    OR `reached the age while the other member has not`
    WHERE
        `reached the age while the other member has not` MEANS
            (`the person has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`)
            AND (`the person is a member of a couple the other member of which has not reached that age`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 15: claimant commitment, date and method of acceptance.

-- (1), (3) A person who has accepted a claimant commitment within the period after making a claim that the Secretary of State
-- specifies is treated as having accepted it on the first day of the period for which the claim is made. The Secretary of State may
-- extend the period where the person asks for a review of a work search or work availability requirement, or of a limitation, and
-- the Secretary of State considers the request reasonable.
-- src:384 | (1) For the basic condition in section 4(1)(e) of the Act, a person who has accepted a claimant commitment within such period after making a claim as the Secretary of State specifies is to be treated as having accepted that claimant commitment on the first day of the period in respect of which the claim is made.
-- src:386 | (3) The Secretary of State may extend the period within which a person is required to accept a claimant commitment or an updated claimant commitment where the person requests that the Secretary of State review—
-- src:387 | (a) any action proposed as a work search requirement or a work availability requirement; or
-- src:388 | (b) whether any limitation should apply to those requirements,
-- src:389 | and the Secretary of State considers that the request is reasonable.
@ref reg 15(1) and (3) (src:384-389)
GIVEN `first day of the period in respect of which the claim is made` IS A DATE
      `day on which the person accepted a claimant commitment` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `last day of the period that the Secretary of State specifies for accepting a claimant commitment` IS A DATE
      `last day of the period as extended by the Secretary of State under paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 15(1) — the day on which the claimant commitment is treated as accepted` `first day of the period in respect of which the claim is made` `day on which the person accepted a claimant commitment` `last day of the period that the Secretary of State specifies for accepting a claimant commitment` `last day of the period as extended by the Secretary of State under paragraph (3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `day on which the person accepted a claimant commitment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST accepted THEN
        IF accepted AT MOST `last day of the period allowed`
        THEN JUST `first day of the period in respect of which the claim is made`
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `last day of the period allowed` MEANS
            CONSIDER `last day of the period as extended by the Secretary of State under paragraph (3)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `last day of the period that the Secretary of State specifies for accepting a claimant commitment`
            WHEN JUST extended THEN
                IF extended GREATER THAN `last day of the period that the Secretary of State specifies for accepting a claimant commitment`
                THEN extended
                ELSE `last day of the period that the Secretary of State specifies for accepting a claimant commitment`

-- (2) Where an award may be made without a claim, a person who accepts a claimant commitment within the period the Secretary of State
-- specifies is treated as having accepted it on the day that would be the first day of the first assessment period in relation to the
-- award in accordance with regulation 21(3) or (3A).
-- src:385 | (2) In a case where an award may be made without a claim, a person who accepts a claimant commitment within such period as the Secretary of State specifies is to be treated as having accepted a claimant commitment on the day that would be the first day of the first assessment period in relation to the award in accordance with regulation 21(3) or (3A).
@ref reg 15(2) (src:385)
GIVEN `the day that would be the first day of the first assessment period in accordance with regulation 21(3) or (3A)` IS A DATE
      `day on which the person accepted a claimant commitment` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `last day of the period that the Secretary of State specifies for accepting a claimant commitment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 15(2) — the day on which the claimant commitment is treated as accepted where an award may be made without a claim` `the day that would be the first day of the first assessment period in accordance with regulation 21(3) or (3A)` `day on which the person accepted a claimant commitment` `last day of the period that the Secretary of State specifies for accepting a claimant commitment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `day on which the person accepted a claimant commitment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST accepted THEN
        IF accepted AT MOST `last day of the period that the Secretary of State specifies for accepting a claimant commitment`
        THEN JUST `the day that would be the first day of the first assessment period in accordance with regulation 21(3) or (3A)`
        ELSE NOTHING

-- (4) A person must accept a claimant commitment by one of the following methods, as the Secretary of State specifies: electronically,
-- by telephone, or in writing.
-- src:390 | (4) A person must accept a claimant commitment by one of the following methods, as specified by the Secretary of State—
-- src:391 | (a) electronically;
-- src:392 | (b) by telephone; or
-- src:393 | (c) in writing.
@ref reg 15(4) (src:390-393)
DECLARE `Method of accepting a claimant commitment` IS ONE OF
    `electronically`
    `by telephone`
    `in writing`

-- src:390 | (4) A person must accept a claimant commitment by one of the following methods, as specified by the Secretary of State—
-- src:391 | (a) electronically;
-- src:392 | (b) by telephone; or
-- src:393 | (c) in writing.
@ref reg 15(4) (src:390-393)
GIVEN `method used` IS A `Method of accepting a claimant commitment`
      `method specified by the Secretary of State` IS A `Method of accepting a claimant commitment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 15(4) — the claimant commitment was accepted by the method the Secretary of State specified` `method used` `method specified by the Secretary of State` MEANS
    `method used` EQUALS `method specified by the Secretary of State`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 16: claimant commitment, exceptions.

-- (1) and (2) A person does not have to meet the basic condition to have accepted a claimant commitment if the Secretary of State
-- considers that they cannot accept one because they lack the capacity to do so, or that there are exceptional circumstances in
-- which it would be unreasonable to expect them to accept one; or if the person is terminally ill.
-- src:395 | (1) A person does not have to meet the basic condition to have accepted a claimant commitment if the Secretary of State considers that—
-- src:396 | (a) the person cannot accept a claimant commitment because they lack the capacity to do so; or
-- src:397 | (b) there are exceptional circumstances in which it would be unreasonable to expect the person to accept a claimant commitment.
-- src:398 | (2) A person does not have to meet the basic condition to have accepted a claimant commitment if the person is terminally ill.
@ref reg 16 (src:395-398)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State considers that the person cannot accept a claimant commitment because they lack the capacity to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State considers that there are exceptional circumstances in which it would be unreasonable to expect the person to accept a claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN  -- keel: regulation 2 defines this; the seat passes in the result of `reg 2 — terminally ill`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16 — the person does not have to meet the basic condition to have accepted a claimant commitment` `the Secretary of State considers that the person cannot accept a claimant commitment because they lack the capacity to do so` `the Secretary of State considers that there are exceptional circumstances in which it would be unreasonable to expect the person to accept a claimant commitment` `the person is terminally ill` MEANS
    (`the Secretary of State considers that the person cannot accept a claimant commitment because they lack the capacity to do so`)
    OR (`the Secretary of State considers that there are exceptional circumstances in which it would be unreasonable to expect the person to accept a claimant commitment`)
    OR (`the person is terminally ill`)
